From f64552f893c83ee5909d33c7919bc9841ad028dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:25:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] orchestration: model-agnostic assessments configured from the
 environment

Questions and answers are our own shapes (yesno/choice/score, plus an
explicit refused answer). Provider adapters translate them: systemone
(TypeSafe /v1/systemone, also Microsoft-Decision-1 on Foundry) and openai
(/v1/decisions). DECISION_PROVIDER, DECISION_BASE_URL, DECISION_MODEL,
DECISION_API_KEY, DECISION_PATH and DECISION_AUTH_HEADER configure it,
with TYPESAFE_* and OPENAI_API_KEY as fallbacks. The provider and model
are recorded in each assessment operation, so changing either replays the
step as changed. The QuickJS host's allowlist follows the configured base
URL. @typesafe-ai/sdk is replaced by a small transport with the same retry
policy.

assessment.test.ts rewritten as one-rule specs: 1,399 -> 892 lines,
60 -> 76 cases. Live checks per provider are opt-in via
CODEMOD_LIVE_ASSESSMENT=systemone,openai.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
